```js
const flat = parts.map((p) => (p.index ? p.toNonIndexed() : p));
const merged = mergeGeometries(flat, false);
flat.forEach(p => p.dispose());
```
But if p was converted, disposing both original and converted? Original parts array items still indexed; dispose them too. Do `parts.forEach(p=>p.dispose())` and `flat.forEach(p=>{ if(!parts.includes(p)) p.dispose(); })` — messy. Just dispose all unique via Set.

Also RoundedBoxGeometry may use groups? toNonIndexed preserves groups. merge with useGroups false ignores groups? It warns? fine.

